{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC3 gate results under the NEW ruff 0.16.3 / mypy 2.3.1 — all green with ZERO source changes:\n\n  make lint          -> ruff check: All checks passed; ruff format --check: 2156 files already formatted; plus config-ownership, config-reads, DCO-identity, criteria-vocabulary, skill-frontmatter, zizmor (no findings), actionlint — all pass\n  make typecheck     -> Success: no issues found in 575 source files\n  make config-check  -> all infra configs valid\n  uv lock --check    -> lock is current (exit 0)\n  tests/e2e          -> 12 passed\n\nCOMPLEXITY RATCHET (run directly, not just via make lint):\n  python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check\n  -> active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0   (exit 0)\n\nThat is the required new=0 increased=0 stale=0. Note the stale=0 specifically: ruff 0.16.3 scores every one of the 49 baselined symbols IDENTICALLY to 0.16.2, so there is no shrink-side drift either. .github/complexity-baseline.json is UNMODIFIED (not in the commit diff).\n\nThe newer mypy and ruff surfaced NO new findings anywhere in the tree. Consequently no fix was needed, and — per the ticket's explicit constraint — no # noqa, no # type: ignore, and no per-rule exclusion was added. The diff is exactly the two files in file_impact: pyproject.toml (1 line) and uv.lock (+81/-73).\n\nAlso checked: .pre-commit-config.yaml does NOT pin ruff/mypy separately — its lint and typecheck hooks are local repos that shell out to 'make lint' / 'make typecheck', so they pick up the venv's locked versions and needed no companion bump."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787195360602888001,"uuid":"863fc502-5f96-46f9-bd63-52c2d110c75f"}